7:**R1 - major - Following a rule remains an English course.**
13:Concrete fix: retain the training/interpretation mechanism but replace the grammar syllabus with visible rule-following problems: continue a sequence, encounter a rival continuation beyond a boundary, distinguish a rule's expression from its application, and establish a correction practice. Assess and recap those distinctions. Preserve the explicit warning that a finite simulated pupil cannot establish the whole argument of PI sections 185-202.
15:**R2 - major - A unique solution to a puzzle is presented as a requirement of propositions.**
21:Concrete fix: distinguish the philosophical point from the extra communication-puzzle constraint: a proposition determines conditions under which it is true; this particular partner additionally needs enough information to choose one position. Retain multiple satisfying arrangements elsewhere and explicitly compare the two cases.
23:**R3 - major - The explanation of doubt wrongly requires the disputed thing to exist.**
29:Concrete fix: explain that some uses of words and practices of checking must stand fast for a particular doubt to operate. Add an ordinary existence question to demonstrate that this is not a ban on doubting whether something exists.
31:**R4 - major - The beetle and hinges are quizzes about activities the player never performs.**
37:Concrete fix: make the core argument playable. For the beetle, let a public task continue while inaccessible contents vary; for the diary, let the player attempt consistent correction under different criteria; for certainty, let them conduct a check and discover what that check relies on. Use the current questions as reflection after those actions.
39:**R5 - major - The implementation does not carry through the selected Notebook composition.**
45:Concrete fix: implement the chosen composition: compact desktop title/deck, portrait cutout and paper edges, visible seven-stop illustrated path, restrained scene height, and the same editorial typography and illustration treatment across games, completion cards and reading pages. Adapt this to the phone without shrinking readable text or touch targets. No alternative direction is being requested by this review.
47:**R6 - major - Phone success and feedback are placed after the content they should explain.**
53:Concrete fix: order phone completion content as completion state, concise learned idea, next/replay actions, then the passage and detailed recap. Keep feedback adjacent to the selection and reveal it after an answer while preserving focus. Check long quotations as well as short ones. A working-tree scroll change exists, but its presence is not evidence that the served build is fixed.
55:**R7 - major - Enter overrides the focused control and records an unintended wrong answer.**
61:Concrete fix: preserve native Enter/Space behavior on buttons, links, summary controls and radios. Scope game-level Enter to the noninteractive background or explicit primary action. Verify stones, quantity controls, destinations, hints and retries. Also expose the shortcut-disable setting in the empty notebook; its current early return hides it from newcomers.
63:**R8 - major - Reset progress does not survive another open tab.**
69:Concrete fix: persist a reset generation or equivalent tombstone. Receiving tabs must replace stale saves and discard drafts, and a stale write must not reintroduce pre-reset records. Recheck the exact two-tab sequence.
71:**R9 - minor - Pupil's first-time accuracy label actually includes teaching efficiency.**
77:**R10 - minor - Notebook retains answers without the philosophical explanation or passage.**
83:**R11 - minor - The first beetle answer requires an unstated restriction.**
89:**R12 - minor - English quotations lead to German-only source texts.**
93:**R13 - minor - One quotation silently modernizes the checked edition's spelling.**
97:**R14 - minor - Demonstrative reference and teaching a new name are conflated.**

